    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31460" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴσομαι</span></b> , fut. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶδα</span> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εἴδω</span>). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Ep.
			
			fut. of (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝ</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εί-</span> 'rush', 'hasten', 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεῦρ᾽ εἴσεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					15.213
				</span></i>
			 : 3sg.
			aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴσατο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.538
				</span></i>
			, etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐείσατο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					15.415
				</span></i>
			; but sts. simply <i>go,</i> as 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					16.313
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάλιν εἴσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.462
				</span></i>
			, al. : c. inf.
			fut., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐεισάσθην συλήσειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					15.544
				</span></i>
			.</div>
